# Job Description Analysis — CSE Curriculum Audit

## 1. Purpose

Compare the curriculum's existing subjects with employer-listed skills to identify strengths and possible learning gaps relevant to early-career technology roles.

## 2. Job Postings Reviewed

| Employer | Role | Date / Experience | Source |
|---|---|---|---|
| TE Connectivity | Data Engineer I | Posted 23 October 2026; designed for 2026 graduates | https://careers.te.com/job/DATA-ENGINEER-I/161077-en_US/ |
| DXC Luxoft | Junior AI/ML Engineer | Posted 21 October 2026; junior role | https://career.luxoft.com/jobs/junior-aiml-engineer-28443 |
| New Street Technologies | Associate Software Engineer | Early-career role; 0–1 year experience | https://newstreettech.com/careers/associate-software-engineer |

## 3. Skills Comparison

| Skill or area | Employer evidence | Related curriculum subject | Initial assessment |
|---|---|---|---|
| Programming and problem-solving | Python, programming fundamentals, data structures | Computer Programming; Data Structures; Object Oriented Programming Concepts | Existing foundation; practical depth should be reviewed |
| SQL and relational databases | SQL, query design, joins, relational databases | Database Management System | Strong subject alignment; verify advanced practical coverage |
| Data pipelines and ETL/ELT | Pipeline development, data processing, data quality | Big Data Systems; Database Management System | Potential area for more hands-on practice |
| AI and machine learning | ML frameworks, model training and evaluation | Artificial Intelligence; Machine Learning | Relevant subjects; verify deployment and evaluation exercises |
| Generative AI | LLMs, RAG, embeddings, vector databases, prompt engineering | Artificial Intelligence; Machine Learning | Potential curriculum enhancement area |
| Software testing | Testing, debugging, code quality | Software Testing; Software Engineering | Existing foundation; verify automated testing practice |
| Version control and collaboration | Git, project work, teamwork | Industry Coding Practices; Special Project | Verify whether Git workflows and code reviews are assessed |
| Cloud and deployment | Cloud platforms are listed as useful skills in the data-engineering role | Cloud Computing | Existing subject; verify practical deployment experience |

## 4. Preliminary Findings

1. The displayed curriculum already includes important foundations such as programming, data structures, databases, algorithms, AI, machine learning, software engineering, testing, big data, and cloud computing.
2. The reviewed postings emphasize applying these foundations through working projects, reliable data pipelines, testing, and version control.
3. Modern AI application development introduces additional topics such as RAG, embeddings, vector databases, and evaluation.
4. These postings suggest opportunities to strengthen practical labs and project-based assessment rather than automatically adding many new courses.
5. The evidence comes from three selected job postings. It is a useful sample, not a statistically representative survey of the entire job market.

## 5. Limitations

- Job descriptions represent specific employers and roles.
- Job requirements can change before 2030.
- The curriculum mapping is preliminary and based on course titles; detailed syllabi and lab exercises must be checked before confirming a gap.
- The job postings do not establish that any particular course should be removed.

## 6. Next Step

Use the curriculum inventory and job evidence to prepare a course-by-course KEEP, UPDATE, REDUCE, or ADD audit, with a reason and evidence reference for each recommendation.
